      cost 6 under gt1030 (the round trip as written would be 6; folded it is 0 and does not round)
    proof:
      1. between 2^-14 and 2^16 the f16 values of a binade are the f32 values whose 13 low mantissa
         bits are 0; the bit pattern grows with |x| and a carry out of the mantissa is the next
         binade's first value, so rounding the value to f16 (nearest, ties to even) is rounding
         the pattern to a multiple of 2^13 (nearest, ties to the even quotient)
      2. (b + 4095 + (b >> 13 & 1)) & ~8191 is that rounding of b, for every 32-bit b: against
         q = b >> 13, r = b mod 2^13, (q + (r > 2^12 or r = 2^12 and q odd)) << 13: proved by SAT (both sides bit-blasted)
      3. the range: every operand is 0 or has 2^-14 <= |x| < 65520, so no result is subnormal or
         infinite and the carry never reaches the sign bit
    check (not the proof): 726 bit patterns, both signs, exponent fields 126..130, ties and their
      neighbours at every mantissa bit: all equal to the evaluator's round trip
    not applied: it costs more than the folded round trip; `foldproof` (simplify ... foldproof) writes it into the module
